---
import meImage from '../../assets/me.png';
import PixelLabel from '../ui/PixelLabel.astro';
import Screw from '../ui/Screw.astro';
import Polaroid from '../ui/Polaroid.astro';
import CraftingGrid from './CraftingGrid.astro';

/**
 * The player card, continued: one fused sheet instead of three pinned notes
 * joined by arrows. Three internal zones carry the same paper/ink/dashed
 * material language as before, but read as one continuous document - the
 * photo bleeds off its edge rather than sitting in an isolated corner.
 */
---

<section class="chunk-grid container-page py-16 lg:py-24" aria-label="About me">
  <div class="spread">
    <div class="sheet">
      <Screw class="top-3 left-4" />
      <Screw class="top-3 right-4" />

      <div class="zone zone--recipe">
        <PixelLabel as="h2" class="mb-4">Crafting Recipe</PixelLabel>
        <p>
          Finished school right in the middle of the pandemic. Officially: Abitur with a focus on
          health and care. Unofficially: full-time gaming, thanks to homeschooling. That's exactly
          when I slid into programming. My motivation: why farm something for hours when a script
          can just do it for me?
        </p>
        <p>
          The interest in programming ended up outgrowing the one in health and care. So in 2021 I
          started an apprenticeship as a software developer. Today I'm a <strong>software architect</strong>
          and <strong>trainer</strong>, and an <strong>IHK examiner</strong> on the side. And I still write
          code on a handful of personal projects.
        </p>
        <CraftingGrid />
      </div>

      <div class="zone zone--chunk">
        <PixelLabel as="h2" class="mb-4">Outside the Chunk</PixelLabel>
        <p>
          Neither gaming nor programming has gotten any less interesting over the years. Honestly, I
          often build more in my free time than at work. My biggest project right now is
          <a href="https://github.com/maik-hasler/einsatzbereit">Einsatzbereit</a>, an attempt at building
          a regional platform for volunteer work.
        </p>
        <p>
          When I'm not coding, I'm probably playing Path of Exile 2. Otherwise I love board and card
          games, Magic: The Gathering especially these days. I love eating just as much, but hate
          cooking. I enjoy running and I'm training for the Oldenburg Marathon (not going well). And
          I read tech books, watch videos, and listen to podcasts about software development.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="zone zone--why" id="why">
        <PixelLabel as="h2" class="mb-4">Why a Piston?</PixelLabel>
        <p>
          One thing has become clear over time: with me, it's binary. 0 or 1. Exactly like a piston.
          Either I'm completely obsessed with something and forget to eat, sleep, or talk to another
          human being, or I'm the exact opposite and do nothing at all.
        </p>
        <p>There's rarely an in-between. Mostly it's just the transition from one extreme to the other.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spread__photo">
      <Polaroid
        src={meImage}
        alt="Maik Hasler wearing a cap and glasses, black-and-white photo"
        caption="The Minecraft Block IRL"
        label="Texture Pack"
        rotate={2}
        size="lg"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .spread {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3rem;
  }
  .spread__photo {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .spread {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 22rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .spread__photo {
      justify-content: flex-end;
      margin-left: -4rem;
      margin-top: 3rem;
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
    }
  }

  /* One object: single rotation, single shadow, single pair of pins - the
     zones inside only differ by background and top seam, never by their own
     transform, so this reads as one continuous sheet, not three cards. */
  .sheet {
    position: relative;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-stone);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    transform: rotate(-0.4deg);
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .sheet {
      transform: rotate(-0.8deg);
    }
  }

  .zone {
    padding: 2.25rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 66ch;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
    hyphens: auto;
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .zone {
      padding: 2.5rem 2.75rem;
    }
  }
  .zone + .zone {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .zone p + p {
    margin-top: 0.85em;
  }
  .zone a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-redstone-bright);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .zone a:hover {
    color: var(--color-redstone);
  }

  .zone--recipe {
    background: var(--color-paper-light);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  .zone--recipe strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .zone--chunk {
    background: var(--color-ink);
    color: var(--color-cream-muted);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-stone);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .zone--chunk a:hover {
    color: var(--color-redstone-bright);
  }

  .zone--why {
    background: var(--color-paper-dark);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--color-stone-light);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
